{{also|rúg}}
==English==

===Etymology===
Origin uncertain; compare Swedish {{term|lang=sv|rugg||rough entangled hair}}, Old Norse {{term|rogg}}, English {{term|rough}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{enPR|rŭg}}, {{IPA|/rʌɡ/}}, {{X-SAMPA|/rVg/}}
* {{rhymes|ʌɡ}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# A small covering for a floor.
#: Note that '''rug''' and '''[[carpet]]''' are not synonymous; ''rug'' covers part of the floor, a ''carpet'' covers most or a large area of the floor; a fitted carpet runs wall-to-wall.
# {{Australia|British}} A (usually thick) piece of [[fabric]] used for [[warmth]] (especially on a bed); a [[blanket]].
# {{slang}} A [[wig]]; [[hairpiece]].

====Synonyms====
* {{italbrac|small carpet}}: [[carpet]], [[mat]]
* {{italbrac|wig}}: [[toupee]], [[wig]]

====Derived terms====
* [[area rug]]
* [[cut a rug]]
* [[scatter rug]]
* [[snug as a bug in a rug]]

